            <div xml:id="d697">

                <pb facs="0806" n="694" xml:id="pg694"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13244: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-29T12:00:00+08:00">October 29,
                        1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received October 29—9:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>101. Following telegram has been received from the Ambassador at Shanghai.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“October 28, 4 p.m. Reference Hankow’s October 26, noon, and October 27, 11
                        a.m. regarding condition in Tatsienlu. I have today addressed note to
                        Foreign Office requesting protection of Americans in area.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
